# The radial, the right trackpad and live bezel and shader switching on the Deck, off-screen:
#   input-check.sh PAD radial-check.cases OUT     (input-check.sh --plan radial-check.cases shows every timeline)
# SYSTEM EMULATOR CORE|- FIRST TOKEN... -- ROM-GLOB; see input-check.sh. A key: token is a radial slot,
# typed as XTest from the private gamescope's second Xwayland; move: and tap: are the right
# trackpad (relative pointer motion and a click, at fractions of the touch screen as drawn); bare
# names are Steam's virtual pad (the replica). The chords are input.json's (config/input/
# linux-desktop): Next Bezel Ctrl+Shift+B, Next Shader Ctrl+Shift+V, Next Slot Ctrl+K, Previous
# Slot Ctrl+J, Menu Ctrl+M, Screenshot Ctrl+X, Shader On/Off Ctrl+H, Bezel On/Off Ctrl+B, Fit
# Ctrl+Shift+F, Aspect Ctrl+Shift+G, Controller Layout Ctrl+Shift+C, Restart Game Ctrl+Shift+D,
# Players Ctrl+Shift+U, Reset to Default Ctrl+Shift+R, and the held menu ring's Up, Down, Confirm and
# Back Ctrl+Up, Ctrl+Down, Ctrl+Space and Ctrl+Backspace. The quick ring's Settings slot and the
# settings radial's Close are Steam preset switches, which only Game Mode can show; every slot of the
# settings radial types one of these chords (steam_input.json settings_slots), so the cases cover
# each slot's action. key:A,B presses A, then B a second later, inside the 3 s confirm window of
# Reset, the one choice that asks twice; no choice restarts the game but Restart Game. No case saves
# or loads a state (a standalone emulator keeps its states in the owner's state root); the choices
# land in OUT/home/semu.json and later cases start from them, so keep the order. Journal codes
# (result "journal", action/slot[/reserved]): 1 menu, 2 up, 3 down, 4 confirm, 5 back, 9 screenshot,
# 77 next slot, 78 previous slot, 79 bezel (slot = the index into the variants file), 80 shader,
# 81 fit, 82 aspect, 83 layout, 84 pad, 85 reset, 86 players page (slot 1 open, 0 back, -1 one
# player), 87 restart (slot 1 restarting, 0 nothing to apply); a third number is the record's
# reserved field: the player plus 16 while its layout waits for Restart Game (83), the player (84),
# 1 while the output waits for Restart Game (82), 1 on Reset's prompt and on a Reset that leaves
# something waiting (85).
#
# 1. "listening for keys on X display"; visual.bezel.next, visual.shader.next, state.next,
#    state.prev and ui.screenshot each once "(keyboard)", nothing deduplicated; journal 79/1 80/1
#    77/1 78/0 9/0; switch receipts naming the arctic shell (bezel_index=1) and the AGB-001 preset
#    (shader_index=1); BEZEL: ARCTIC in after-1, the arctic shell from then on; the game still moving
#    after Ctrl+K (frame advance is cleared); choices gba {"bezel_variant":"arctic","shader_variant":"agb001"}.
gba retroarch mgba 30 key:ctrl+shift+b key:ctrl+shift+v key:ctrl+k key:ctrl+j key:ctrl+x -- Legend of Zelda, The - The Minish Cap (USA).zip
# 2. The launch receipt already draws the arctic shell and AGB-001 (the saved choice); ui.menu
#    "(gamepad)" for Select plus the top face button, which Steam's pad sends as BTN_WEST; the menu
#    shot reads BEZEL ARCTIC; A on BEZEL steps to OFF behind the open menu, B closes it; journal 1 3
#    3 3 3 79/2 5; choices gba bezel_variant "none".
gba retroarch mgba 30 select+north dpad_down dpad_down dpad_down dpad_down south east -- Legend of Zelda, The - The Minish Cap (USA).zip
# 3. Taps reach the melonDS core where they land: touch lines "-> surface 1 native" about 128,96
#    and 12.8,172.8; after Next Bezel (large main, second right) the centre tap is again about
#    128,96 (the touch map follows the live layout); arrow-1, -2, -3 and -5 ok: Semu's arrow at the
#    pointer in cursor-N (1.5 s after the token), none in idle-N (5 s after).
nds retroarch melonds 40 move:0.5,0.5 tap:0.5,0.5 tap:0.05,0.9 key:ctrl+shift+b tap:0.5,0.5 -- Legend of Zelda, The - Phantom Hourglass*.zip
# 4. Standalone Azahar through the Vulkan layer: "semu-vulkan: touch X,Y -> 1 160,120" before and
#    after Next Bezel; the toast and the new layout composed; arrow-1, -2 and -4 ok: Semu draws its
#    arrow over Azahar too (semu_pointer_sample), and cursor-N (type 3, gamescope's cursor plane
#    included) shows that one arrow, Azahar's own cursor blank on its render widget.
n3ds azahar - 50 move:0.5,0.5 tap:0.5,0.5 key:ctrl+shift+b tap:0.5,0.5 -- Legend of Zelda, The - Ocarina of Time 3D*.3ds
# 5. The Semu menu over a standalone that keeps running under it (Azahar menu.pause none): Ctrl+M
#    opens it (journal 1, ui.menu "(keyboard)", Azahar's own Ctrl+M mute is blanked), the pad moves
#    it (3, 2) and A on RESUME closes it (5). The menu holds the pad while it is open (follow-up F1):
#    the launch log says "the menu holds 1 pad(s)" then "gave 1 pad(s) back", and the title must not
#    advance in after-4, since neither the d-pad nor that A reached Azahar.
n3ds azahar - 50 key:ctrl+m dpad_down dpad_up south -- Legend of Zelda, The - Ocarina of Time 3D*.3ds
# 6. The Azahar core reads x as 0.1 + 0.8 f of its 400-wide frame: core x about 0.14, 0.50, 0.86.
n3ds retroarch azahar 50 tap:0.05,0.5 tap:0.5,0.5 tap:0.95,0.5 -- Legend of Zelda, The - Ocarina of Time 3D*.3ds
# 7. The Citra core reads the pointer as its touch screen (citra_touch_touchscreen): the tap registers.
n3ds retroarch citra 50 tap:0.5,0.5 -- Legend of Zelda, The - Ocarina of Time 3D*.3ds
# 8. DeSmuME takes the tap at the pointer (desmume_pointer_type touch), not at its own relative cursor.
nds retroarch desmume 40 tap:0.5,0.5 -- Legend of Zelda, The - Phantom Hourglass*.zip
# 9. Ctrl+H steps the shader to OFF (80/2) and no longer resets the game (the shots keep moving);
#    Ctrl+M opens and closes the menu (1, 5) and loads no RetroArch shader.
psx retroarch mednafen_psx 45 key:ctrl+h key:ctrl+m key:ctrl+m -- Crash Bandicoot (USA).m3u
# 10-12. Standalone emulators act on the radial's slot chords themselves (their own selected-slot
#    hotkeys: Dolphin and PCSX2 show slot 2 then 1, PPSSPP its slot) while Semu journals 77/1 78/0 and
#    toasts SLOT 2 / SLOT 1; then Next Bezel or Next Shader switches live (79/1 or 80/1).
gc dolphin - 50 key:ctrl+k key:ctrl+j key:ctrl+shift+b -- Legend of Zelda, The - The Wind Waker (USA).rvz
ps2 pcsx2 - 60 key:ctrl+k key:ctrl+j key:ctrl+shift+v -- Devil May Cry (USA).iso
psp ppsspp - 45 key:ctrl+k key:ctrl+j key:ctrl+shift+b -- Daxter*.iso
# 13. A system without bezels: visual.bezel.next "(keyboard)" then "no bezel to choose for wiiu
#     here"; journal 79/-1 (the toast BEZEL: NONE HERE); nothing saved; Cemu keeps running.
wiiu cemu - 100 key:ctrl+shift+b -- MARIO KART 8 (US).wua
# 14. Radial v2 on a two-player system with one layout and one output, steered by the held menu
#     ring's chords: Controller Layout journals 83/-1 (CONTROLLER: ONE LAYOUT) and Aspect 82/-1
#     (ASPECT: ONE ONLY), nothing saved; Players opens the menu (1) on its players page (86/1; the
#     page shot reads P1 PAD 1, P2 NO PAD, RESTART GAME, BACK); Ctrl+Down to P2 (3), Ctrl+Space finds
#     no free pad for it (84/-1/1), Ctrl+Up back to P1 (2); Ctrl+Backspace returns to the menu on its
#     PLAYERS row (86/0) and again closes the menu (5); each chord "(keyboard)" once.
snes retroarch snes9x 30 key:ctrl+shift+c key:ctrl+shift+g key:ctrl+shift+u key:ctrl+down key:ctrl+space key:ctrl+up key:ctrl+backspace key:ctrl+backspace -- Super Mario World (USA).zip
# 15. Bezel On/Off, Fit and Reset on a handheld (case 2 left the gba bezel OFF and case 1 the AGB-001
#     shader): Ctrl+B brings the default shell back (79/0), Fit shows the whole shell at a whole step
#     (81/0, FIT: BEZEL), Ctrl+B turns it off again (79/2); the first Reset prompts (85/0, RESET: PRESS
#     AGAIN) and the second, a second later, journals 79/0 80/0 81/1 85/1 (RESET TO DEFAULTS): the
#     default shell, the default shader and the screen fit come back live, and OUT/home/semu.json has
#     no gba entry left under visual.systems or input.systems.
gba retroarch mgba 30 key:ctrl+b key:ctrl+shift+f key:ctrl+b key:ctrl+shift+r,ctrl+shift+r -- Legend of Zelda, The - The Minish Cap (USA).zip
# 16. The Wii's own choices, none of which restarts the game by itself: Controller Layout steps P1
#     from the default Nunchuk to Classic live (83/2, P1: CLASSIC, the log line "P1 layout classic: 1
#     press(es) of Alt+F5 via X" and Dolphin's own "profile 'Semu' for device 'Wiimote1'" message),
#     then to GameCube, which Dolphin reads at boot (83/3/16, P1 GAMECUBE: RESTART TO APPLY, nothing
#     typed, the game still moving), then on to Wii Remote, live again from the Classic still running
#     (83/0, one more Alt+F5); Fit steps the placement live (81 and its FIT: toast); Players opens the
#     menu (1) on the page (86/1: P1 PAD 1 WII REMOTE, P2-P4 NO PAD), and two Ctrl+Backspace return to
#     the menu (86/0) and close it (5); one Aspect press saves visual.games.wii.<game>.output =
#     widescreen in OUT/home/semu.json (82/1/1, ASPECT 16:9: RESTART TO APPLY) with the game still
#     running, and Restart Game (87/1, RESTARTING GAME) restarts it once in the same launch
#     (restarts=1), the new argv (cmdline) holding --config SYSCONF.IPL.AR=True.
wii dolphin - 60 key:ctrl+shift+c key:ctrl+shift+c key:ctrl+shift+c key:ctrl+shift+f key:ctrl+shift+u key:ctrl+backspace key:ctrl+backspace key:ctrl+shift+g key:ctrl+shift+d -- New Super Mario Bros. Wii*.wbfs
